# Multi-run table -- EXAMPLE, not a template. Nothing copies this file; write your own.
# The manual explains it: https://ozankiratli.github.io/PoolSeqFlow/
#
# To use one: in parameters.config set multiRun = true and multiRunFile = 'your-table.csv'.
# Blank lines and # lines are ignored, so a run can be kept commented out instead of deleted.
#
# THE RULES:
#   1. One column must be RunID. It becomes a directory under storageDir, so letters, digits,
#      dot, dash and underscore only.
#   2. Every other column is a parameter name spelt as parameters.config spells it, with no
#      `params.` prefix. Nested ones are dotted: trim_galore.quality, variantCall.maxDepth.
#      Any parameter may be varied. A name that is not one is refused, not ignored.
#   3. A blank cell takes the value from parameters.config, so the table is only as long as
#      the difference between the runs.
#   4. Quote a value containing a comma: "-a AD,DP,SP,INFO/AD". The default readPattern,
#      *_R{1,2}.fq.gz, is one.
#
# Setting an INPUT re-derives whatever depends on it: poolSize moves sensitivity, threads
# moves the whole cores ladder. Setting a COMPUTED value pins it, and its inputs stop feeding
# it -- pin variantCall.mpileupOptions and variantCall.maxDepth no longer means anything for
# that run. Step 0 names any column that does this.

# A real, usable table: two references, the second trimmed harder. Delete or replace it.
RunID,referenceFile,gffFile,trim_galore.quality
reference_a,reference_a.fasta.gz,reference_a.gff.gz,
reference_b,reference_b.fasta.gz,reference_b.gff.gz,30
